  "result": "The `drv.motion.at_rest` concept passed the gate (`OK`) on the first run, so 5 of the 6 runs are left.\n\n**The concept.** It holds when the road user's speed is at or below the speed tolerance at the observation. It doesn't look at the brake lamp, the brake input or any place:\n```lean\ndef body : Formula :=\n  .cmp (.measure \"kin_speed\" [aA]) .le pSpeedTolerance\n```\nThe contract's \"at or below\" maps straight onto `.le`, so I made no reading choices and declared no narrowings.\n\n**The witnesses.** The speed tolerance is set to 0.1 m/s. Each scenario has one vehicle (track 1) observed at three instants one second apart:\n- **holds:** speed 0 m/s, and the gate judged it compliant.\n- **fails:** speed 10 m/s with the brake lamp lit, judged violated.\n- **blind:** the same stopped vehicle as in `holds`, with `kin.speed` declared absent in both the trace and the manifest, judged unknown.\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory. The record had no problems to report.",
